{"company":{"id":"google-search","name":"Google Search","accent":"#4285f4","asset":"the index","verb":"search"},"nodes":[{"id":"client","title":"Search box / client","kind":"client","blurb":"Query string or pan/zoom.","depth":0,"story":"This is the Google Search app on your phone or laptop. Tapping search starts here. The app does not hold the whole product — it only starts the request."},{"id":"dns","title":"DNS + edge","kind":"cdn","blurb":"Nearest frontend.","depth":0,"story":"Your phone asks “where is the nearest Google Search door?” DNS points at a close edge so the first hop is short."},{"id":"fe","title":"Frontend / web server","kind":"api","blurb":"Renders results, spells, UI.","depth":1,"story":"The page or app shell for Google Search search. It is not the entire index."},{"id":"api","title":"Query service","kind":"api","blurb":"Normalizes the query.","depth":1,"story":"Think of this as Google Search’s front desk. The app asks it for “what’s allowed / what’s next,” not for huge the index. It routes, limits traffic, and hides internal stores."},{"id":"spell","title":"Spell / suggest","kind":"service","blurb":"Autocomplete as you type.","depth":2,"story":"“Did you mean…?” as you type. A small service around the same query."},{"id":"rank","title":"Ranking","kind":"service","blurb":"IR + signals → order.","depth":2,"story":"Which story is on top. Signals (who you care about, what you watched) — not a random shuffle."},{"id":"ads","title":"Ads (if any)","kind":"service","blurb":"Optional auction beside organic.","depth":2,"story":"If Google Search shows ads, that auction sits beside organic results — it is not the index."},{"id":"cache","title":"Results cache","kind":"cache","blurb":"Popular queries and tiles.","depth":3,"story":"The same questions get asked thousands of times (session, “is this still available?”). Google Search keeps those answers in fast memory so the main database is not hit every time."},{"id":"index","title":"Inverted / tile index","kind":"db","blurb":"The thing you actually search.","depth":3,"story":"The lookup book. This is what a query actually searches, not a scan of every page."},{"id":"doc","title":"Document / place store","kind":"db","blurb":"Snippets, titles, geometry.","depth":4,"story":"Snippets, titles, places — the text you see under a result."},{"id":"crawlq","title":"Crawl / ingest queue","kind":"queue","blurb":"New pages, mail, or map edits.","depth":5,"story":"New pages wait to be fetched. Crawling is not done while you press Search."},{"id":"crawler","title":"Crawlers / ingest","kind":"workers","blurb":"Fetch and parse offline.","depth":5,"story":"Fetches and parses pages in the background so the index can stay fresh."},{"id":"indexw","title":"Index builders","kind":"workers","blurb":"Rebuild shards continuously.","depth":6,"story":"Rewrites index shards from the raw corpus. Continuous, not on your keystroke."},{"id":"blob","title":"Raw corpus","kind":"blob","blurb":"Original pages, mail, or imagery.","depth":6,"story":"The warehouse for large the index. Cheap to store, not great for “show my last 20 items.” Google Search points at these files from the records database."},{"id":"knowledge-graph","title":"Knowledge graph","kind":"service","blurb":"Connects entities so a result can understand that “Jaguar” may be a car or animal.","depth":6,"story":"Connects entities so a result can understand that “Jaguar” may be a car or animal."}],"edges":[{"from":"client","to":"dns","label":"nearest POP"},{"from":"dns","to":"fe","label":"HTML / app"},{"from":"fe","to":"api","label":"the query"},{"from":"api","to":"spell","label":"did you mean"},{"from":"api","to":"rank","label":"order results"},{"from":"rank","to":"cache","label":"popular q"},{"from":"rank","to":"index","label":"lookup"},{"from":"rank","to":"ads","label":"auction"},{"from":"index","to":"doc","label":"snippets"},{"from":"crawlq","to":"crawler","label":"new URLs"},{"from":"crawler","to":"blob","label":"raw pages"},{"from":"crawler","